Compared with 1.10.0, the release before it:

- Five new GGUF pipelines, experimental, in the "Ensemble Mode" tab
  (Pipeline menu, group "Experimental, open to feedback"): reazonspeech,
  kotoba, whisper-turbo, whisper-large and MOSS. Japanese only. CrispASR,
  which runs them, is updated to 0.8.50.
- ChronosJAV (Qwen3-ASR, anime-whisper) now times each subtitle by its VAD
  group by default. No aligner and no timing model run unless you choose
  them under "Customize Parameters".
- "Finish each file" is on by default: an Ensemble run finishes each file
  before the next one starts, and loads each pass's models again for every
  file.
- Fixed: the Qwen3-ASR fine-tunes JA Anime-Galgame and JA-tuned writing
  random text (#494). The timing model, when you choose it, is no longer
  given audio under 0.2 s (#498, #500); a very short stretch inside longer
  audio can still cause the crash.
- Fixed in AI translation (#460): answer labels in other languages, such as
  Chinese, left in the translation. Subtitles the model did not translate
  are now named by number and the run ends with TRANSLATION INCOMPLETE;
  they are still left out of the translated file.
- Each GUI run writes a log file, raw_subs\whisperjav_run.log, in the output
  folder; while "Save next to source video" is ticked, next to the first
  item in the file list (inside it, if that item is a folder). Each run
  replaces the last.
- Not fixed yet: ZipEnhancer cleans only the first file of a single-pass
  run, and of an Ensemble run with "Finish each file" unticked. Planned for
  1.10.2.

