-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THIS INSTALL IS MADE FOR
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Each install is made for one accelerator, chosen when you install:

- NVIDIA GPU (CUDA): chosen without a question on a PC with an NVIDIA card
  of the GTX 16 series, RTX 20 series or newer, and driver 580 or newer.
  Every pipeline uses the GPU.
- GPU through Vulkan: for an AMD, Intel or older NVIDIA card. The GGUF
  pipelines ask for the card through Vulkan (experimental, not yet tested
  on AMD or Intel cards); the other pipelines run on the CPU, several times
  slower. If Vulkan is not found on the PC, the CPU-only version is
  installed.
- Own PyTorch (advanced): WhisperJAV installs everything except PyTorch.
  You add your PyTorch build with the command the installer shows at the
  end; it is also saved in OWN_PYTORCH_NEXT_STEP.txt in the install folder.
  Until you have run it, every WhisperJAV command stops and shows it again.
- CPU only: every pipeline runs on the CPU (not accelerated).

The choice is kept in whisperjav_stack.txt in the install folder; every run
and every upgrade follow it. To change it, run the installer again into the
same folder: it removes the old install, then asks again. On an Own PyTorch
install, add your PyTorch again afterwards.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
YOUR COMPUTER
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit. Windows on ARM is not supported.
- 8 GB RAM (16 GB recommended).
- About 10 GB free disk space, for the install and the models it downloads.
- Internet while installing, and on the first run of each model.
- Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime, for the GUI (if it is missing, the
  installer opens its download page).
- For the GGUF pipelines: a processor with AVX2 (Intel since 2013, AMD since
  2015).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFTER INSTALLATION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The install folder is C:\Users\<you>\AppData\Local\WhisperJAV by default
(%LOCALAPPDATA%\WhisperJAV), or the folder you chose.

To check the install, open Command Prompt (press Start, type cmd, press
Enter) and run:
  cd /d "%LOCALAPPDATA%\WhisperJAV"
  Scripts\whisperjav.exe --version
  Scripts\whisperjav.exe --check
(If you chose another folder, put it in the first line.)
The first prints "WhisperJAV {{VERSION}}". The second names the install's
accelerator and where each part runs.

Files in the install folder:
  install_log_v{{VERSION}}.txt              the installation log
  whisperjav_stack.txt                 what the install is made for
  OWN_PYTORCH_NEXT_STEP.txt            Own PyTorch only: the command to run
  INSTALLATION_STOPPED_v{{VERSION}}.txt     only if the installer stopped on
                                       purpose: the reason
  INSTALLATION_FAILED_v{{VERSION}}.txt      only if the installation failed:
                                       the reason
  WhisperJAV-GUI.exe                   the GUI launcher

Your settings (%APPDATA%\WhisperJAV) and your downloaded models
(%USERPROFILE%\.cache) are outside the install folder. The exception: the
XXL Faster Whisper settings "Executable" and "Extra Args" are saved inside
it, so enter them again after you reinstall.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UPGRADING TO A LATER 1.10 RELEASE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The GUI tells you when a new version is out; it does not upgrade by itself.

1. Close WhisperJAV (every window of it).
2. Open Command Prompt and run:
     "%LOCALAPPDATA%\WhisperJAV\python.exe" -m whisperjav.upgrade
   (if you installed into another folder, use that folder instead).
3. When it asks "Continue? [y/N]:", type y and press Enter.
4. When it says "Upgrade complete!", check the version:
     "%LOCALAPPDATA%\WhisperJAV\Scripts\whisperjav.exe" --version

Do not start the upgrade with "whisperjav-upgrade" or
Scripts\whisperjav-upgrade.exe, although the tool's own messages name it:
when WhisperJAV is installed on another drive than Windows' temporary
folder (normally drive C:), it stops halfway and WhisperJAV no longer
starts.

When the upgrade finishes, it suggests "whisperjav-upgrade --rollback". Do
not use it: on installs made with this installer it stops with an error.

If WhisperJAV no longer starts after an upgrade, uninstall it (see below)
and install the newest release with the installer. Your settings and
downloaded models stay; enter the XXL Faster Whisper "Executable" and
"Extra Args" again.

Do not update with "pip install -U whisperjav": on Windows it can replace
your GPU build of PyTorch with a CPU-only one.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UNINSTALLING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Open Windows Settings > Apps, find WhisperJAV and choose Uninstall, or
double-click Uninstall-WhisperJAV.exe in the install folder. After an
upgrade, the Apps entry still names the version you first installed.

The uninstall leaves the desktop shortcut; delete it yourself. Your settings
(%APPDATA%\WhisperJAV) and downloaded models (%USERPROFILE%\.cache) also
stay. To free the space, delete %APPDATA%\WhisperJAV, and in
%USERPROFILE%\.cache the model folders you no longer need; other programs
may keep files there too.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TROUBLESHOOTING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- The installation failed: install_log_v{{VERSION}}.txt names the phase that
  failed, and INSTALLATION_FAILED_v{{VERSION}}.txt holds the reason. Run the
  installer again; it offers to replace the partial install.
- "no supported NVIDIA GPU found" although you have an NVIDIA card: the
  window names the reason. For an old driver, or a card WhisperJAV cannot
  reach: update or repair the driver, restart the PC and run the installer
  again. For a card older than 1.10 supports, the window names WhisperJAV
  1.9.5, which still supports it.
- A run stops with "THE NVIDIA GPU CANNOT BE USED" (in the GUI, a window
  titled "The NVIDIA GPU cannot be used"): it names the reason and the fix.
  In the GUI, "Run on the CPU this time" runs that job on the CPU; on the
  command line, add --device cpu.
- The GUI does not open, or its window is blank: install WebView2 from
  https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/p/?LinkId=2124703
- Downloads fail or time out: check the connection; behind a firewall,
  allow python.exe, uv.exe and git.exe. Users in China: keep your VPN on
  during the whole installation, during an upgrade, and on the first run of
  each model (models come from huggingface.co).
- An antivirus program blocks the downloads: add an exclusion for the
  install folder, or pause real-time scanning while installing.

More help:
https://meizhong986.github.io/WhisperJAV/guides/installation_windows_standalone/#troubleshooting

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND LINE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The command-line programs are in the Scripts folder of the install folder.
In Command Prompt, in the install folder:
  Scripts\whisperjav.exe "D:\Videos\movie.mp4" --mode balanced
  Scripts\whisperjav.exe --help
  Scripts\whisperjav-translate.exe --help
The subtitles are written next to the video.

Command-line reference:
https://meizhong986.github.io/WhisperJAV/user-guide/cli-reference/

